  data:  # 1878
    kind: invariant  # 1878
    title: "C taint: a source a callee copies into a global config struct, later sent through a function pointer, is never followed (torsocks SOCKS5 password and getpid/time username); host-secret-no-network reads confirmed_with_caveats once INV-zikul classifies every call"  # 1878
    status: violated  # 1878
    priority: 2  # 1878
    parent:  # 1878
    tags:  # 1878
    - c  # 1878
    - taint  # 1878
    - verify_claims  # 1878
    - false_confirm  # 1878
    isbefore: []  # 1878
    duplicate_of: []  # 1878
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 1878
    pr_ref:  # 1878
    description: "FOUND 2026-10-04 in the INV-zikul-kikov-nikig-dovig-naros-sagik-bufil-punub A/B (branch jgstern-agent/fix/zikul). Pre-existing taint gap; the INV-zikul fix UNMASKS it on torsocks, it does not cause it.\n\nWHAT. torsocks sends a host secret and a host description over the network, and C taint does not follow either flow:\n  - host_secret: src/lib/torsocks.c:125 password = getenv(DEFAULT_SOCKS5_PASS_ENV) -> conf_file_set_socks5_pass(password, &tsocks_config) copies it into the GLOBAL tsocks_config.conf_file.socks5_password -> a different function later passes the global's fields to socks5_send_user_pass_request (src/common/socks5.c:284) -> memcpy into buffer -> send_data(conn->fd, buffer, data_len) at :325, where send_data is a FUNCTION POINTER (socks5.c:146) to send_data_impl -> send(). The same function also logs the password: DBG(\"Socks5 username %s and password %s sent successfully\", user, pass) (:333), and DBG is a macro over log_print, emitted as the unresolved call c:external:0-0:DBG.\n  - host_description: src/common/config-file.c:528-534 pid = getpid(); now = time(NULL); snprintf(config->conf_file.socks5_username, ..., \"torsocks-%ld:%lld\", pid, now) -> the same SOCKS5 send.\nSo host-secret-no-network, host-description-no-network and host-secret-no-logging are false.\n\nWHY IT SURFACES NOW. On the base (c1dd831558) these torsocks verdicts were inconclusive ONLY because the coverage gate listed 6 unclassifiable modules (arpa/inet, assert, common/log, common/utils, lib/torsocks, +1): those came from the incomplete C include stamp on connect/send/close. With the stamp fixed every call classifies, nothing withholds, and the verdicts read confirmed_with_caveats (launch caveat only: autoreconf, mkdir). Verdicts that move this way on torsocks: host-secret-no-network, host-description-no-network, host-secret-no-logging (false by reading the code above), untrusted-input-no-host-fs (a received SOCKS5 reply byte is logged through DBG to the log file when TORSOCKS_LOG_FILE_PATH is set: a flow, if a thin one), untrusted-input-no-subprocess and untrusted-input-no-database (no flow found by reading; torsocks' C code launches nothing and has no database).\n\nThe withholding that hid this was claiming something false (\"calls the catalogue could not classify\") once the stamp is right, so restoring it is not the fix. The fix is in taint (a source stored into a global/struct by a callee and read by another function; calls through a function pointer; macro-wrapped logging), or a disclosure that withholds a taint clean when the flow-relevant constructs are present. Related but distinct: INV-komoj (a source RETURNED from a helper)."  # 1878
    fields:  # 1878
      statement: "A taint claim reads clean only if every flow from a catalogued source to a catalogued sink of its zone is either reported or disclosed as unfollowed; a source stored into a global or a struct field by a callee and read by another function, and a sink reached through a function pointer or a logging macro, are flows."  # 1878
      root_cause: "Not diagnosed. Candidates seen in torsocks: the def/use model does not carry taint through a global struct field written by a callee (conf_file_set_socks5_pass(password, &tsocks_config)); the call graph does not follow the send_data function pointer to send_data_impl; DBG(...) is an unexpanded macro, emitted as c:external:0-0:DBG. Until INV-zikul the coverage gate withheld these verdicts for an unrelated reason (incomplete include stamps), which hid the gap."  # 1878
- op: discuss  # b87d
  at: '2026-10-19T18:14:49Z'  # b87d
  by: agent  # b87d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b87d
  clock: 2  # b87d
  nonce: b87d  # b87d
  message: "Progress, 1 of 3 mechanisms: PR (dev 3e7538b5b5) makes a call through a C function-pointer variable reach the function it holds (static ssize_t (*send_data)(...) = send_data_impl). torsocks: all 12 send_data / recv_data calls now reach the _impl functions; redis 20. Fixture getenv -> send_data(...) now reads violated. NOT yet fixed: torsocks' host-secret-no-network still reads clean, because the password reaches the send only through the global tsocks_config a callee stores it into. Plan (owner-approved 2026-10-19): the next PR is a DISCLOSURE that withholds a C taint clean when a source's value reaches a construct the walk does not follow (a store into non-local memory, a function-like macro call, a project varargs parameter). Actually following each construct is filed as separate items."  # b87d
- op: discuss  # df29
  at: '2026-10-19T18:17:44Z'  # df29
  by: agent  # df29
  actor: jgstern_agent  # df29
  clock: 3  # df29
  nonce: df29  # df29
  message: "Trackerized per owner (2026-10-19): actually following each construct is filed as WI-nulam (out-parameter: a callee writing through a pointer param), WI-zitul (cross-function global state), WI-ropab (function-like macro expansion) and WI-ronuj (variadic tail -> va_list sink). This item continues with the DISCLOSURE."  # df29
- op: discuss  # eee0
  at: '2026-10-19T18:22:21Z'  # eee0
  by: agent  # eee0
  actor: jgstern_agent  # eee0
  clock: 4  # eee0
  nonce: eee0  # eee0
  message: "DESIGN for the disclosure PR. Four unfollowed-site kinds, stamped by c.py on CALL edges as meta unfollowed_construct (a new edge-meta key):\n- out_parameter_call: a call to a project function that writes through one of its pointer params. A pass-1 summary per function: an assignment rooted at a pointer param, or a copy-family call (strcpy/strlcpy/strncpy/memcpy/snprintf...) whose destination roots at one.\n- non_local_store: a copy-family call whose destination roots at the caller's own pointer param or a file-scope variable.\n- macro_call: an unresolved call whose name is a function-like macro the file can see (its include closure).\n- variadic_call: a call to a variadic project function with arguments in its ... tail.\ntaint (propagate_taint_ddg): from each source site, the existing three-valued walk runs with the stamped call lines of that function as pseudo-sinks. A reached site is an unfollowed escape for the source's label. verify_claims: a taint claim on that label that would read clean reads INCONCLUSIVE, with a caveat naming the sites. The scope is per label, not per zone, because where the value went is unknown.\ntorsocks, by reading: the password reaches conf_file_set_socks5_pass(password, &tsocks_config), whose body does strlcpy(config->...socks5_password, password) -> out_parameter_call. The username is snprintf(config->conf_file.socks5_username, ..., pid, now) with config a pointer param -> non_local_store. A plain assignment store (g = v;) is not a call and is a later PR."  # eee0
- op: discuss  # 1000
  at: '2026-10-19T20:36:30Z'  # 1000
  by: agent  # 1000
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1000
  clock: 5  # 1000
  nonce: '1000'  # 1000
  message: "Progress, 2 of 3: the DISCLOSURE is merged (PR #1740, dev 715cef9165 + 91f91cf287). c.py stamps edge meta unfollowed_construct on four call-site kinds: out_parameter_call, non_local_store (copy-family), macro_call and variadic_call. taint.find_unfollowed_escapes runs the §3a walk from each source site to those sites. verify_claims withholds a clean verdict whose label escaped.\nBehavioral evidence: hypergumbo verify-claims on torsocks (frozen copy) on merged dev:\n- host-secret-no-network: inconclusive (was confirmed_with_caveats). Names torsocks.c:143 and :171, the out_parameter_call conf_file_set_socks5_user/pass(..., &tsocks_config), and :311, a macro_call.\n- host-secret-no-logging: inconclusive (was confirmed_with_caveats), same sites.\n- host-description-no-network: inconclusive (was confirmed_with_caveats). Names config-file.c:532, the non_local_store snprintf(config->...) of getpid / time.\ncrun, tmate and redis moved no verdict.\nSTATUS STAYS violated: a PLAIN assignment to non-local memory (g = getenv(..); c->f = v / *c = v through a pointer param, in the source's own function) is not a call and is not stamped. That is PR 3, next."  # 1000
