- op: discuss  # 1b58
  at: '2026-10-19T22:37:35Z'  # 1b58
  by: agent  # 1b58
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1b58
  clock: 7  # 1b58
  nonce: 1b58  # 1b58
  message: "SATISFIED after three PRs: #(fptr) dev 3e7538b5b5; #1740 dev 715cef9165 + 91f91cf287; #1741 dev 61e61b9055 + 2315eab1bd.\n\nBehavioral evidence: `hypergumbo verify-claims` on merged dev. Claims: SECRET-NO-NET (host_secret -> network) and SECRET-NO-LOG (host_secret -> logging). Every filed shape is now either REPORTED or DISCLOSED.\n  direct: getenv -> send in one function   -> NO-NET violated (reported); NO-LOG confirmed, correct: nothing logs\n  helper: getenv -> send through a helper  -> NO-NET violated (reported)\n  fptr: send through `static int (*send_data)(..) = send_impl`  -> NO-NET violated. REPORTED: a call through a function-pointer variable now reaches the function it holds.\n  global: a callee copies the secret into a global struct (set_pass(p, &g_conf) -> strncpy(c->pass, v)), sent from another function -> NO-NET / NO-LOG inconclusive (disclosed: out_parameter_call)\n  macro: DBG(..) function-like macro over fprintf(stderr, ..)  -> NO-NET / NO-LOG inconclusive (disclosed: macro_call)\n  plain store: g_secret = getenv(..) in one function, send(fd, g_secret) in another  -> NO-NET / NO-LOG inconclusive (disclosed: non_local_store via meta.non_local_store_lines)\n  torsocks (frozen copy): host-secret-no-network, host-secret-no-logging, host-description-no-network -> all inconclusive (were confirmed_with_caveats). The reasons name torsocks.c:143 / :171 (conf_file_set_socks5_user/pass(.., &tsocks_config)), torsocks.c:311 (macro) and config-file.c:532 (snprintf(config->..) of getpid/time).\nCorpus, verify-claims vs dev for each PR: crun, tmate and redis moved no verdict. No over-withholding was measured. The plain-store recording fires on about 29% of their functions.\n\nWhat the fix is: a call-graph fix for function pointers, and a DISCLOSURE for the rest, per owner direction (2026-10-19). The invariant's statement is met: the flow is \"reported or disclosed as unfollowed\". Actually FOLLOWING the disclosed constructs is filed as WI-nulam (out-parameter summaries), WI-zitul (cross-function global state), WI-ropab (macro expansion) and WI-ronuj (variadic tails). When one lands, its construct stops withholding.\n\nNot covered, stated rather than implied:\n- C only. cpp/objc have the same constructs and are not stamped.\n- A store through an ALIAS of a pointer parameter (q = c; q->f = v) is not recorded."  # 1b58
